  "id": "BIT-tomcat-2026-65182",
  "summary": "Apache Tomcat: Bypass longest prefix security constraint",
  "details": "Improper Access Control, Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in Apache Tomcat leads to security constraint bypass if a constraint for a longer path is specified before a more restrictive constraint for a shorter sub-path.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 11.0.0 through 11.0.24, from 10.1.0 through 10.1.57, from 9.0.0 through 9.0.120, from 8.5.0 through 8.5.100, from 7.0.0 through 7.0.109.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 11.0.25, 10.1.58, 9.0.121, which fixes the issue.",
